LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Writing in the Galleries
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, we begin by looking closely at artwork—a
 sking what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Together\, we'll explore w
 hat we think the artist is trying to say and what the social significance
  of their message might be. Then we'll use our imaginations to respond to
  any aspect of our experience. Poets\, story-tellers\, and essayists are 
 all welcome in this group!Read more about The Photographic Reflex: The Le
 e Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/
 exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-deprez.html)  &#160\;  W
 hat to Bringyour favorite pencil (no pens).  a notebook or paper. Clipboa
 rds are available to borrow.  a phone or camera to take a picture of the 
 art for later reference.    &#160\;Know Before You GoArrive early\, check
  in\, and get ready for an on-time start.Readwhere to find us\, where to 
 park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.About Your Facilitator  Deda
 imia Whitney earned an MFA in fiction from Indiana University under the d
 irection of Scott Russell Sanders. She taught creative writing at Frankli
 n College for many years. She has served the museum as a docent since 201
 9. Her favorite works of art are those that are both visually stimulating
  and thought-provoking.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In this workshop\, we begin by looking 
 closely at artwork—asking what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Toge
 ther\, we'll explore what we think the artist is trying to say and what t
 he social significance of their message might be. Then we'll use our imag
 inations to respond to any aspect of our experience. Poets\, story-teller
 s\, and essayists are all welcome in this group!</p><p><a href="https://a
 rtmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-dep
 rez.html">Read more about The Photographic Reflex: The Lee Marks and John
  C. DePrez Jr. Collection</a></p><p>  &#160\;</p><h3>  What to Bring</h3>
 <ul><li>your favorite pencil (no pens).  </li><li>a notebook or paper. Cl
 ipboards are available to borrow.  </li><li>a phone or camera to take a p
 icture of the art for later reference.  </li></ul><p>  &#160\;</p><h3><st
